# Ignore rules for the build context.
#
# The context is sent to the daemon in full before any instruction in the
# Dockerfile runs, so anything listed here was on the daemon's disk and in the
# build cache whether or not a COPY mentions it. That is a different thing from
# "not in the final image", and it is the thing that leaks credentials: a
# file that was excluded from every COPY still lands in a layer the daemon
# holds, and `docker history` on a pushed image will happily tell you so.
#
# So this list is not hygiene, it is the difference between a secret that was
# never transmitted and one that was transmitted and is probably fine.

# --- credentials and operator state ---------------------------------------
# The operator's own config. It names real accounts, real handles, and the
# environment variable their sessionid lives in.
config.toml
config.*.toml
# A proxy list is a paid resource and its addresses are the tool's whole point
# of existing. Mounted at run time, never copied.
proxies.txt
*.proxies.txt
# Anything a sessionid could have been written into by a tool, a shell, or an
# editor's swap file.
*.session
.env
.env.*
*cookie*.txt
*sessionid*
secrets/
config/secrets/

# --- run output -----------------------------------------------------------
# The checkpoint ledger and artifacts. A volume mounts here instead; a ledger
# baked into an image is a ledger nobody can rotate, and one that outlives the
# run that produced it.
runs/
artifacts/
data/
insta-report-data/
state/
traces/
checkpoints/
# The accounts to report. Identifying rather than secret, and bound at run time
# alongside the config.
targets/
targets.txt
*.targets.txt
*.checkpoint.jsonl
*.trace.zip
*.jsonl
!tests/**/*.jsonl

# --- git ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The history contains the operator's real account id in five commits, which
# is precisely why this line matters: the current tree is clean and the
# history is not, and the daemon does not care about the difference.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- development ----------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Not ours, and large.
.claude-flow/
node_modules/

# The legacy single-file scripts are kept in the repo for reference and are not
# importable, so they have no business in a runtime image.
igban.py
get_id.py
